# Source: https://genome.ucsc.edu/FAQ/FAQformat.html#format1
#   https://github.com/arq5x/bedtools2/issues/1078
# Symptom: BED lines have trailing whitespace (spaces or tabs) after the last
#   field; arises from printf/echo without trimming, or copy-paste from
#   spreadsheets.  Strict parsers count the trailing whitespace as an extra
#   empty field, producing "too many columns" or parsing the empty string as
#   the next expected column (e.g. thickStart becoming "").
chr1	100	200	feat001	0	+   
chr1	300	400	feat002	255	-	
chr2	1000	2000	feat003	500	+  
